+config LUOFU_SELECTOR
+	tristate "HiSilicon Luofu A/B boot selector"
+	depends on ARCH_LUOFU || COMPILE_TEST
+	depends on MFD_SYSCON
+	help
+	  Sysfs interface to the A/B boot-selector cell in the SYSCTRL page of
+	  the Hi5671Y "luofu" SoC.  The stock bootloader boots the firmware pair
+	  (kernela + rootfsa, or kernelb + rootfsb) named by the low byte of that
+	  cell and keeps the recorded value sticky across resets.
+
+	  "current_pair" decodes the cell (0x10 = pair A, 0x11 = pair B, plus
+	  the documented manual/recovery and un-initialised states), and
+	  "next_pair" writes one of the two measured recorded-pair values and
+	  verifies the read-back.  The driver shares the SYSCTRL regmap with the
+	  machine-restart driver and performs no register access at probe time:
+	  the cell is only read or written when userspace asks.  It is needed by
+	  the A/B sysupgrade path; say N unless you are building that path.
+
